Marathon Symbiosis update launches December 8, adding new PvE and PvP modes, weapons, and more
Marathon &#8216;s Symbiosis update arrives December 8, bringing new PvE and PvP modes, weapons, a Runner shell, and expanded areas to explore on Tau Ceti IV. Today we’ve got first details on the updated Perimeter zone, Expedition mode, and more.
What&#8217;s new in Marathon: Symbiosis&nbsp;
Players can experience Marathon during Open Play Week, running December 8 &#8211; 15, alongside the launch of Symbiosis.&nbsp;
Marathon is available now on PS5 , with full cross-play and cross-save support.** The Symbiosis update launches December 8 for all players.&nbsp;
**Cross-save requires an internet connection, and for each system you play on: 1) a copy of the Marathon game compatible with your system (other versions sold separately); and 2) system network account linked to your Bungie.net account.
Updated Perimeter zone: Fungal growth and alien life have transformed Perimeter, introducing new playable spaces including the underground Burrows and submerged Reservoir. Runners will also encounter the Tick Queen, who lurks deep beneath the surface.&nbsp;

